<title>FRANCE: Cabin crew of BA TAT unit call 24-hr strike.</title>
<headline>Cabin crew of BA TAT unit call 24-hr strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French SNPNC flight attendants' union said on Thursday it has called members out on a 24-hour strike from Friday midnight, local time, to protest against what it said were constantly deteriorating work conditions.</p>
<p>The Syndicat National du Personnel Navigant Commercial, which said it represents 90 percent of the cabin crew, accuses TAT of undermining quality levels by degrading work conditions, chronic cuts in staffing and use of temporary work contracts.</p>
<p>TAT is a wholly-owned subsidiary of British Airways Plc.</p>
</text>
